  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{(-1)^{4}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
